@startuml f5-secret-resolve
title F5 — Secret resolve at task start (open env surface)

|EX|
start
:Container about to start;
:Have scope_token in hand
 (from F4 handoff);

|EX|
:open env { scope_token } (GET /secrets/open-env);

|Secret Service|
:Validate HMAC signature;
:Validate scope not expired (TTL);
:Validate scope project matches task;
:For each secret_id in scope:
  fetch ciphertext, decrypt in memory;
:Render env-style map
 (e.g. SECRET_A=..., SECRET_B=...);
:Return map;

|EX|
:Receive env-style map;
note right
  Plaintext crosses exactly
  one boundary: SS -> EX.
  Returned in env shape
  (KEY=value) so it can be
  set as container env directly.
end note
:Mount tmpfs in container
 (e.g. /run/secrets/*);
:Write each value as file mode 0400;
:Set SECRET_REFS env var
 (secret_id -> /run/secrets/<id>);
:Set env vars from the map
 (SECRET_A=..., SECRET_B=...);
:Start container process;

|AG|
:Agent SDK reads /run/secrets/* at start;
:Or reads env vars directly;
:Tools read their secret at first use;
:No runtime fetch needed unless refreshed;

stop

note right
  Plaintext only inside the tmpfs / env.
  Gone the moment the container exits.
  GW is not on this path.
end note

@enduml